Parts of this plugin are adapted from TensorFold (bertholomus's fork, github.com/bertholomus/TensorFold, branch
deepseek-v41-tp2) under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the license text: LICENSE at the root of this repository):

  csrc/exl3_l2pf.cu   the paced L2 prefetch kernel, from src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/l2_prefetch.cu (commit f464b09e);
                      our launcher and binding.
  csrc/exl3_rdma.cu   the RDMA all-reduce: rings, flags, doorbell and CPU proxy from TensorFold's one-hop gather
                      (src/tensorfold/cuda/rdma_gather.cu, v5); the fp32 rank-order sum and the vLLM hook (rdma.py) are ours.
  l2pf.py             the prefetch points and their pacing follow TensorFold's design, and so do EXL3_L2PF_ORDER's
                      8 MiB MoE fork (families/deepseek_v41/cuda/model.py L2_MOE_MB, commit bd0024d) and head
                      fork after the last layer (rounds.py _l2_next, commit f464b09e); the code is ours.
  sparse_attn.py      the split-over-keys + ordered-merge structure follows TensorFold's DeepSeek-V4.1 sparse attention
                      (_sparse_attn_part / _sparse_attn_merge); the kernels are ours.
  csrc/exl3_smoe.cu   the shared expert as one more slot of the routed-expert launch is TensorFold's idea; the kernel is ours.
  csrc/exl3_mrow.cu, csrc/exl3_smoe.cu (EXL3_L2_DISCARD)
                      dropping the dead fp32 decode scratch from L2 once summed (discard.global.L2) is TensorFold's
                      idea (commit bd0024d, TF_EXL3_L2_DISCARD); the code is ours.
  csrc/exl3_router.cu (ROUTER_PF), csrc/exl3_mrow.cu (MROW_L2PF)
                      loading or prefetching a kernel's weights before griddepcontrol.wait follows TensorFold's
                      kernels; the code is ours.

Copied unchanged from the same branch at commit 90b68e06 (src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/), TensorFold's EXL3 module (its
decoders follow ExLlamaV3's EXL3 format, MIT, Copyright (c) 2025 Turboderp; see LICENSE.exllamav3):

  csrc/tf_experts/experts.cpp, experts.cu, experts_cb0.cu, experts_cb1.cu, experts_cb2.cu, experts_grouped.cuh
                      the grouped routed-expert kernels; the plugin uses their prompt-chunk path
                      (VLLM_EXL3_MOE_TF_PROMPT=1, tf_prompt.py).
  tf_experts.py       from src/tensorfold/cuda/exl3/experts.py; changed: _ext() builds csrc/tf_experts/ with the
                      plugin's JIT loader (jit.load_dir), marked at the top of the file.

